{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "**Cherry Blossoms and Neon Nights: My Japan Adventure**\n\nStepping off the plane in Tokyo, I was immediately struck by the electric hum of the city. It is a place where ancient tradition and futuristic innovation dance together seamlessly. My journey began in the serene gardens of the Imperial Palace, where the stillness of the pond mirrored the towering skyscrapers beyond.\n\nThe next morning, the Shinkansen whisked me away to Kyoto. Here, time seemed to slow down. Walking through the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove, the sound of wind rustling through the tall stalks created a natural symphony. I visited Kinkaku-ji, the Golden Pavilion, reflecting perfectly in the surrounding pond, a sight that took my breath away.\n\nFood in Japan is an art form. From steaming bowls of ramen in narrow alleyways to the delicate precision of sushi at a tiny counter in Osaka, every bite was a revelation. I still dream about the perfect balance of flavors in a simple onigiri.\n\nOne evening, I got lost in the neon-lit streets of Shinjuku. The energy was palpable, with rain-slicked streets reflecting the vibrant lights of pachinko parlors and izakayas. Despite the crowds, there was a sense of order and politeness that made navigating the chaos surprisingly easy.\n\nLeaving Japan felt like waking from a vivid dream. The blend of history, technology, and unparalleled hospitality left an indelible mark on my soul. Whether you seek the quiet of a Zen temple or the thrill of a bustling arcade, Japan offers an experience unlike any other. I am already counting the days until I can return to this magical land.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.29092026}, {"token": "Ch", "logprob": -0.26571336}, {"token": "erry", "logprob": -0.29458764}, {"token": " Bloss", "logprob": -0.0011481675}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": -1.549722e-06}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -8.011185e-05}, {"token